Additionally, you may want to consider implementing a code review process, where you regularly review and discuss code changes with your team, to ensure that everyone is on the same page and that the codebase remains maintainable and efficient. This can help you identify potential issues early on and make adjustments as needed, rather than trying to make drastic changes later on. 

Remember, maintainability is not a one-time achievement, but rather an ongoing process that requires continuous attention and refinement. By finding a balance between efficiency and readability, and by regularly reviewing and discussing your code, you can ensure that your codebase remains maintainable and efficient over time.

